WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.416
Welcome to the Chronicle Fundamentals Workshop!

2
00:00:03.416 --> 00:00:06.547
Have you ever wondered where your GitHub Copilot

3
00:00:06.547 --> 00:00:09.417
chats go after you close Visual Studio Code?

4
00:00:09.417 --> 00:00:14.374
Every question you ask, every thinking bubble, every command, and every code

5
00:00:14.374 --> 00:00:18.809
change is saved inside a hidden detective notebook on your computer.

6
00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:22.462
Today, in just sixty fun minutes, you are going to build

7
00:00:22.462 --> 00:00:26.115
Chronicle—your very own local web app to explore it all!

8
00:00:27.015 --> 00:00:31.664
Here is our coolest superpower today: the Zero-Package Rule!

9
00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:37.166
Most apps download hundreds of outside mystery boxes from the internet.

10
00:00:37.166 --> 00:00:41.196
If even one box breaks, the whole castle falls down!

11
00:00:41.196 --> 00:00:45.613
Instead, we will build every single piece using the clean

12
00:00:45.613 --> 00:00:50.262
LEGO bricks already built into Node.js and your web browser.

13
00:00:50.262 --> 00:00:55.299
Zero npm installs, zero node_modules, and lightning-fast startup!

14
00:00:56.199 --> 00:01:00.508
We kick off in Lab Zero with an easy seven-minute backpack check.

15
00:01:00.508 --> 00:01:05.479
Check that Node version twenty-two or newer is ready in your terminal, open

16
00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:10.517
the empty sampleapp folder directly in VS Code, and switch Copilot Chat into

17
00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:15.025
Agent mode with a frontier model like Claude Sonnet, GPT, or Gemini!

18
00:01:15.925 --> 00:01:19.162
Next, in Lab One, you paste your first prompt

19
00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:24.989
to create Copilot's magic rulebook: dot-github slash copilot-instructions-dot-md.

20
00:01:24.989 --> 00:01:30.240
From that moment on, VS Code automatically hands your rulebook to Copilot

21
00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.851
on every single prompt—so Copilot remembers never to install outside packages!

22
00:01:36.751 --> 00:01:39.906
In Lab Two, Copilot builds the brain of your app!

23
00:01:39.906 --> 00:01:44.027
It learns how to read both classic VS Code chats and new Copilot

24
00:01:44.027 --> 00:01:49.049
Agent sessions, indexes every word in a speedy background worker, and builds a

25
00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:54.072
Spot-the-Difference engine so deleted lines glow red and new lines glow green.

26
00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:58.901
Then you run node --test and watch green checkmarks light up your terminal!

27
00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:03.755
In Lab Three, you build a fast, private local web

28
00:02:03.755 --> 00:02:10.050
server in src/server.js using Node's built-in http module—no Express required!

29
00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:14.004
It locks the door to 127.0.0.1 so random websites

30
00:02:14.004 --> 00:02:18.281
can never peek at your chats, and automatically finds

31
00:02:18.281 --> 00:02:22.961
your computer's default VS Code and Agent session folders!

32
00:02:23.861 --> 00:02:29.274
Finally, in Lab Four, two fun prompts paint your entire browser playground!

33
00:02:29.274 --> 00:02:34.325
You will create over sixty crisp SVG icons, a Markdown highlighter and

34
00:02:34.325 --> 00:02:39.016
HTML safety shield, easy sorting by Date or Name, and a one-click

35
00:02:39.016 --> 00:02:43.707
toggle between sleek Dark Mode and super-clear Bright White Mode!

36
00:02:44.607 --> 00:02:47.975
At the finish line, use the Node start command in

37
00:02:47.975 --> 00:02:51.550
Lab Four, open the local address it prints, and even

38
00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:55.743
find the very workshop conversation you are having right now!

39
00:02:55.743 --> 00:02:58.217
Open Lab Zero in VS Code, trust your

40
00:02:58.217 --> 00:03:02.273
empty sampleapp folder, and let's build Chronicle together!
